Root changes on insert if the root was originally NULL.

Track duplicates with a count variable to make sure the node hasn't been insterted already.
isEmpty: Check if root is null
findMin: go left until you reach the last node - Tail Recursion
findMax: advance right until you find the last node.
treeHeight: find the max between height of left and height of right, this returns the larger number, which is the height of the tree.

remove: Find max on the right hand side hanging from the node being deleted, get that node and substitute it in the place of the element being deleted.

Tail Recursion: Make a recursive call as the last line of your method; iterating across the data set. Can be replaced with a while loop.

Side Note: 
Underflow --> Remove something from an empty data structure
Underflow --> Search for something in an empty data structure

Scenario 1: Node has two children
-- t.element == x and t.left != null && t.right != null
--- set t.element = findMin ( t.right ).element;
--- set t.right = remove( t.element, t.right );

*** Scenario 2: One Child (left or right) or no children ***
-- t = (t.left != null) ? t.left : t.right;

